    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "6230776c9425422f74c5f70488959fbae330e97aedaf3423d1021c91bded53d0",
      "text": "After breakfast you will have an unforgettable program at the Argentinian side of the Falls.\n\nFoz de Iguassu Falls are located in the National Park with its unique flora and fauna, which appeared after a volcanic eruption, and the displacement of the earth formations. The name Tupi-Guarani Indian tribe is translated from the waterfalls and means \"big water\". There are 275 waterfalls, each of which has its own name, which rush down with a crash into the canyon of \"Devil's Throat\". There is an amazing contrast between the calm and even lazy river water over Iguassu Falls above and the powerful overthrow boiling water flows from a height of 72 meters into the abyss. You can stand for hours without stopping, watching this show and thinking about the magnificence of the universe and eternity. Transfer back to hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1jgHNRDGUx9imoBuqYXFJ87xPUwHxZIsY",
        "documentSha256": "c8ebdd8c617fd65a257104b3da99ffbbbb8d7205cf16ffebfb5cdc209a27853a",
